A||||3||87GT||Restoring Stock Rims?||||5||
Z||000000||87GT||01-19-2001||01:49 PM||||I recently got new A/R Carrera Rims for my fiero but I dont want to part with my stock rims.  I replaced them because they were looking pretty rough.  I was wondering if anybody knows of how or where to have these rims restored to perfection?  Thanks for any input. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fformula88||01-19-2001||03:31 PM||||Try a quick search.  There were a few posts about this very thing not too long back.  I have refinished the 14" Fiero rims, but not with the brushcoat finish they originally had.  I sanded out all of the pitting and took off all the clear coat.  Then polished them up with aluminum polish until they had a mirror like finish.  To protect it I sprayed them with clear engine paint (to resist the heat from the brakes).  If interested, I'll be glad to post more detailed instructions.  <P>------------------<BR>John<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">    <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||01-19-2001||03:43 PM||||Go to  <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/wheel.htm" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroproject.com/wheel.htm</A> <BR>There are a couple of other links there, too.<P>Also check out the rest of the site... <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroproject.com</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||JetroGT||01-20-2001||08:31 AM||||TransWheel does a very nice job. They bead blast the wheel then recut it. After that they powder coat it in ither black gray or gold. I don't know if they do any other color.||||reg||14
